Say which state the game is in, and what a menu token was.

A port is debugged from a log and a screen, and the screen only shows what a state managed
to draw - so a transition that happened and rendered nothing looks exactly like one that
never happened. That cost an evening: pressing Play appeared to restart the menu, and
whether it had reached the name screen, reached the level select and bounced, or never
fired at all could not be told apart from outside the machine.

With these two lines it took one run. The log read

    state: st_title -> st_name     the name screen was reached
    state: st_name  -> st_set      the name was accepted
    state: st_set   -> st_title    and the level select bounced straight off

which is a different problem from the one it looked like, and named it precisely: the level
select returns to the title on `GUI_BACK` and nothing else, so something was sending a
second activation. It was - the SDK was delivering every keypress twice.

The addresses resolve against `build/neverball.map`, where every `st_*` is a symbol. The
token line names what a menu screen was asked to do, which is the same question one level
further in.

diff --git a/ball/st_set.c b/ball/st_set.c
index 5a96176..51e4374 100644
--- a/ball/st_set.c
+++ b/ball/st_set.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "util.h"
 #include "common.h"
+#include "log.h"
 
 #include "game_common.h"
 
@@ -46,6 +47,12 @@ enum
 
 static int set_action(int tok, int val)
 {
+    /* **Which token, and how many sets there were to choose from.** This screen returns to the
+     * title on `GUI_BACK` and on nothing else, so when Play appeared to bounce straight off it
+     * the question was only ever whether something sent `GUI_BACK` or whether the screen had
+     * nothing to show. One line answers it; `GUI_BACK` is 1, `SET_SELECT` is `GUI_LAST`. */
+    log_printf("set_action: tok=%d val=%d total=%d\n", tok, val, total);
+
     audio_play(AUD_MENU, 1.0f);
 
     switch (tok)
diff --git a/share/state.c b/share/state.c
index d0c2dcd..697fb4b 100644
--- a/share/state.c
+++ b/share/state.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "video.h"
 #include "common.h"
+#include "log.h"
 #include "hmd.h"
 #include "geom.h"
 
@@ -125,6 +126,15 @@ int goto_state(struct state *st)
 {
     struct state *prev = state;
 
+    /* **Every state change, named by address.** A port is debugged from a log and a screen, and
+     * the screen only shows what a state managed to draw - so a transition that happens and
+     * renders nothing looks exactly like one that never happened. That cost most of an evening:
+     * pressing Play appeared to restart the menu, and whether it had reached the name screen or
+     * bounced off it could not be told apart from the outside. The addresses resolve against
+     * build/neverball.map, where every `st_*` is a symbol. */
+    log_printf("state: %p -> %p (enter=%p)\n",
+               (void *) prev, (void *) st, st ? (void *) st->enter : NULL);
+
     if (state && state->leave)
         state->leave(state, st, state->gui_id);
 
